AIP v2 Master Reference Doc — Practices, Permissions, Approvals, Referrals, Chat
0) What changed from v1 → v2
v1 (current)

Doctors are the primary public directory entity.

Institutions exist, but doctors mostly drive everything.

Join requests are mostly “Doctor membership requests” approved by Admin.

Doctor portal exists (profile, locations, insurance, appointments, referrals, membership).

Admin portal manages requests, members (doctors), plans, policies, events.

v2 (new)

Practices (clinics) become the primary entity.

Doctors belong to a practice.

Doctors can join an existing practice OR create a new practice.

If a doctor creates a practice, they become Practice Admin (extra permissions).

Approval flows become multi-party:

Admin approval always required

Practice Admin approval required for doctors joining that practice

Referral + notification layer expands.

Chat feature planned and must be considered in data model + permissions.

