3) New Approval Workflows (Critical)

We need clarity in Admin approval screens.

3.1 Scenario A — Doctor joins an existing practice (doctor picks practice)

Flow:

Doctor signs up:

selects an existing practice

submits doctor info

Status becomes: pending_practice_admin_approval + pending_admin_approval

Practice Admin reviews and approves/denies

Admin reviews and approves/denies

Only when both approve:

doctor becomes Active

doctor appears in directory under that practice

doctor portal access granted

If either rejects → request rejected (store reason + who rejected)

3.2 Scenario B — Doctor creates a new practice (becomes Practice Admin)

Flow:

Doctor chooses “Create new practice”

They fill:

Practice info

Then their doctor profile info (as practice admin)

Submit creates “PracticeCreationRequest” (new join request type)

Admin reviews:

Approve → practice created + doctor created as active practice admin

Reject → nothing created; applicant notified

Important:

Practice Admin profile becomes active ONLY after Admin approval.

3.3 Scenario C — Practice Admin invites/adds a doctor

Flow:

Practice Admin adds doctor basic details (name + email) → creates “Invitation”

System sends email invitation (future; for now create a record + show link)

Doctor signs up via invitation link:

practice preselected

Approval required:

Admin approval required (always)

Practice admin approval could be auto-approved since invite originated from practice admin (configurable)

But per your requirement: still treat as approval flows if needed

3.4 Practice edits by practice admin (needs admin approval)

Practice Admin requests changes:

practice name/description/contact

practice locations

insurance/services

Admin sees pending “PracticeEditRequest”
Admin approves → apply overrides to practice data

